From 487357e427204f898f5d1ef66725cd769af4c823 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CyberNeko-AI <cyberneko.ai@aosc.io>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 14:55:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 79/79] video_fb: Add integer scaling support

Add a framebuffer scaling factor so that rendering can happen in a
logical resolution smaller than the physical mode. This is useful on
high-DPI portrait panels: the physical mode stays at the native
resolution, avoiding firmware scaler artifacts, while GRUB renders
into a logical screen of width/scale x height/scale and expands each
logical pixel into a scale x scale block on the framebuffer.

The scaling factor is read from the "fb_scale" environment variable
and combined with the rotation transform. For example, on a
1600x2560 panel, "set rotation=270; set fb_scale=2" renders a
1280x800 landscape UI.

- Add a scale field to grub_video_mode_info.
- Divide the logical (post-rotation) dimensions by the scale.
- Apply the scale in the framebuffer transform helpers (fbutil) and
  in the slow blitters (fbblit), which expand each logical pixel to a
  scale x scale block on the framebuffer.
- Add a GRUB_FB_SCALE option to grub-mkconfig.
- Fix scaled and rotated framebuffer scrolling and add regression coverage.

This commit is authored with assistance from AI/LLM:

